-- National Insurance Law [Consolidated Version], s 334 (פרשנות) — interpretation for Chapter 15,
-- insurance contributions. Quotations (`src:N`) are copied mechanically from line N of
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/national-insurance-law-consolidated-version-5755-1995.he.wiki.txt.
--
-- WHICH YEARS IT ANSWERS (NOTES.md, assumption A1). s 334 carries one amendment tag, תשפ״ה־7,
-- which counts to the Law for the 2025 budget year (Sefer HaChukim 5785 p. 395); that Law's own
-- s 21 says its National Insurance chapter commences on 1 January 2026, and its s 19(2) is what
-- inserts the definition of the reduced collection threshold (verified against the enacted PDF,
-- Repair 2026-10-07). So the text below is the text in force from 1 January 2026. What it said before is not in the sources, and a month
-- before 2026 is declined by name rather than answered from the amended text.

§ `Section 334 — interpretation`
-- src:3598 | פרק ט״ו: דמי ביטוח
-- src:3599 | סימן א׳: הוראות כלליות
-- src:3601 | סעיף 334 – פרשנות [תיקון: תשפ״ה־7]

-- The vintage refusal, shared by every rule below that is asked about a year before 2026.
@ref National Insurance Law s 334, amendment tag at source line 3601; the 2025 budget-year Law s 19(2) (inserting the definition) and s 21 (commencement 1 January 2026), Sefer HaChukim 3384, pp. 395-396, PDF at ../../registers/source-bundle/amending-laws/25_lsr_6133485.pdf
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 334(a) as it stood before 1 January 2026 is not in the deposited text` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 334(a) as it stood before 1 January 2026 is not in the deposited text"

§§ `334(a) — "payment period" and "payment date"`

-- src:3602 | (א) בפרק זה –
-- src:3603 | ”תקופת תשלום“ – פרק זמן שלפיו משתלמים דמי ביטוח;
-- src:3604 | ”מועד תשלום“ – מועד לתשלום דמי ביטוח;
-- Carriers of words: no rule in this row computes with either. How long a payment period is, is
-- s 336 (a month, unless the Minister sets otherwise), and when payment is due is set outside this
-- row; both are out of scope (NOTES.md coverage table).
@ref National Insurance Law s 334(a), "תקופת תשלום" (source line 3603)
GIVETH A STRING
`s 334(a) — "payment period"` MEANS "a period of time by which insurance contributions are paid"

@ref National Insurance Law s 334(a), "מועד תשלום" (source line 3604)
GIVETH A STRING
`s 334(a) — "payment date"` MEANS "a date for the payment of insurance contributions"

§§ `334(a) — "reduced collection threshold"`

-- src:3605 | ”מדרגת גבייה מופחתת“ – סכום של 7,522 שקלים חדשים [note: (נקוב לשנת 2025; בשנת 2026, 7,703 ש״ח)], כשהוא מעודכן ב־1 בינואר של כל שנה כלהלן:
-- src:3606 | (1) בשנים 2026 עד 2028 – לפי שיעור עליית המדד שפורסם לאחרונה לפני 1 בינואר, לעומת המדד שפורסם לאחרונה לפני 1 בינואר של השנה הקודמת;
-- src:3607 | (2) משנת 2029 ואילך – לפי שיעור עליית השכר הממוצע, המעודכן ב־1 בינואר, לעומת השכר הממוצע ב־1 בינואר של השנה הקודמת.
-- "a sum of 7,522 NIS, as updated on 1 January of every year as follows: (1) in the years 2026 to
-- 2028 – by the rate of rise of the index last published before 1 January, compared with the
-- index last published before 1 January of the previous year; (2) from 2029 on – by the rate of
-- rise of the average wage as updated on 1 January, compared with the average wage on 1 January
-- of the previous year."
--
-- The note "(נקוב לשנת 2025; …)" is the editors'; the text itself says only that the sum is
-- updated each 1 January under (1) from 2026, which makes 7,522 the figure the first update
-- starts from. Nothing here rounds the updated figure (NOTES.md, fork F7); the Institute's
-- published 2026 figure is in whole shekels. A fall in the index or the wage: fork F6, a switch
-- from version 0.4.0 (below); before it, the fall was applied as the formula gives it.
@ref National Insurance Law s 334(a), "מדרגת גבייה מופחתת" (source line 3605)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the sum printed in section 334(a)` MEANS 7_522

§§ `334(a)(1)-(2) — a fall in the index or the average wage (fork F6; version 0.4.0)`

-- (1) "לפי שיעור עליית המדד", by the rate of RISE of the index; (2) "לפי שיעור עליית השכר הממוצע", by
-- the rate of rise of the average wage (source lines 3606-3607). Neither paragraph says what follows
-- when the later reading is lower than the earlier. Three readings are kept by name (nouns,
-- `A reading of section 334(a) where the index or the average wage falls`): the fall is applied as
-- the formula gives it (this row's reading in versions 0.1.0 to 0.3.1); the threshold stays where
-- it was; the case is declined. RULED by Meng on 2026-10-07 (TRIDENT): declined by default, this
-- row's rule being to decline where the text does not decide. The switch is the rule below; the
-- other readings are a one-line change there. A rise, or no change, is answered the same under all
-- three readings.
@ref National Insurance Law s 334(a)(1)-(2) (source lines 3606-3607); fork F6; Meng's ruling of 2026-10-07 (TRIDENT)
GIVETH A `A reading of section 334(a) where the index or the average wage falls`
`section 334(a) — the reading this row takes where the index or the average wage falls` MEANS
    `a fall is declined`

@ref National Insurance Law s 334(a)(1)-(2) (source lines 3606-3607); fork F6
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 334(a) updates the threshold by the rate of rise of the index or of the average wage, and says nothing of a fall` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 334(a) updates the threshold by the rate of rise of the index or of the average wage, and says nothing of a fall"

-- "the rate of rise of X, compared with Y": (X − Y) / Y, and the sum is updated by that rate. Where
-- X is below Y, the reading decides.
@ref National Insurance Law s 334(a)(1)-(2) (source lines 3606-3607); fork F6
GIVEN `the sum before the update` IS A NUMBER
      `the earlier reading`       IS A NUMBER
      `the later reading`         IS A NUMBER
      r                           IS A `A reading of section 334(a) where the index or the average wage falls`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the sum` `the sum before the update` `updated by the rate of rise from` `the earlier reading` `to` `the later reading` `, reading a fall as` r MEANS
    IF   `the later reading` AT LEAST `the earlier reading`
    THEN `the formula`
    ELSE CONSIDER r
         WHEN `the fall is applied`              THEN `the formula`
         WHEN `the threshold stays where it was` THEN `the sum before the update`
         WHEN `a fall is declined`               THEN `section 334(a) updates the threshold by the rate of rise of the index or of the average wage, and says nothing of a fall`
    WHERE
        `the rate of rise` MEANS (`the later reading` MINUS `the earlier reading`) DIVIDED BY `the earlier reading`
        `the formula`      MEANS `the sum before the update` PLUS `the sum before the update` TIMES `the rate of rise`

-- The rule of versions 0.1.0 to 0.3.1, by its old name, now at the reading the switch names.
@ref National Insurance Law s 334(a)(1)-(2) (source lines 3606-3607); the switch above
GIVEN `the sum before the update` IS A NUMBER
      `the earlier reading`       IS A NUMBER
      `the later reading`         IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the sum` `the sum before the update` `updated by the rate of rise from` `the earlier reading` `to` `the later reading` MEANS
    `the sum` `the sum before the update` `updated by the rate of rise from` `the earlier reading` `to` `the later reading`
        `, reading a fall as` `section 334(a) — the reading this row takes where the index or the average wage falls`

@ref National Insurance Law s 334(a)(1) (source line 3606)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 334(a)(1) updates the threshold by the index only on 1 January 2026, 2027 and 2028` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 334(a)(1) updates the threshold by the index only on 1 January 2026, 2027 and 2028"

@ref National Insurance Law s 334(a)(2) (source line 3607)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 334(a)(2) updates the threshold by the average wage only from 1 January 2029` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 334(a)(2) updates the threshold by the average wage only from 1 January 2029"

-- (1): the index readings are the consumer price index "last published before 1 January" of the
-- year, and of the year before; they are inputs (s 1 "the index", nii-s1-definitions.l4).
@ref National Insurance Law s 334(a)(1) (source line 3606); fork F6
GIVEN `the year`                                           IS A NUMBER
      `the threshold of the year before`                   IS A NUMBER
      `the index last published before 1 January of the year before` IS A NUMBER
      `the index last published before 1 January of the year`        IS A NUMBER
      r                                                    IS A `A reading of section 334(a) where the index or the average wage falls`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 334(a)(1) — the threshold on 1 January of` `the year` `from` `the threshold of the year before` `by the index from` `the index last published before 1 January of the year before` `to` `the index last published before 1 January of the year` `, reading a fall as` r MEANS
    IF   `the year` AT LEAST 2026 AND `the year` AT MOST 2028
    THEN `the sum` `the threshold of the year before` `updated by the rate of rise from` `the index last published before 1 January of the year before` `to` `the index last published before 1 January of the year` `, reading a fall as` r
    ELSE `section 334(a)(1) updates the threshold by the index only on 1 January 2026, 2027 and 2028`

@ref National Insurance Law s 334(a)(1) (source line 3606); the switch above
GIVEN `the year`                                           IS A NUMBER
      `the threshold of the year before`                   IS A NUMBER
      `the index last published before 1 January of the year before` IS A NUMBER
      `the index last published before 1 January of the year`        IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 334(a)(1) — the threshold on 1 January of` `the year` `from` `the threshold of the year before` `by the index from` `the index last published before 1 January of the year before` `to` `the index last published before 1 January of the year` MEANS
    `s 334(a)(1) — the threshold on 1 January of` `the year` `from` `the threshold of the year before` `by the index from` `the index last published before 1 January of the year before` `to` `the index last published before 1 January of the year`
        `, reading a fall as` `section 334(a) — the reading this row takes where the index or the average wage falls`

-- (2): the average wage "as updated on 1 January" of the year, and on 1 January of the year
-- before; published figures, so inputs (s 1 "the average wage"; NOTES.md fork F5).
@ref National Insurance Law s 334(a)(2) (source line 3607); fork F6
GIVEN `the year`                                       IS A NUMBER
      `the threshold of the year before`               IS A NUMBER
      `the average wage on 1 January of the year before` IS A NUMBER
      `the average wage as updated on 1 January of the year` IS A NUMBER
      r                                                IS A `A reading of section 334(a) where the index or the average wage falls`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 334(a)(2) — the threshold on 1 January of` `the year` `from` `the threshold of the year before` `by the average wage from` `the average wage on 1 January of the year before` `to` `the average wage as updated on 1 January of the year` `, reading a fall as` r MEANS
    IF   `the year` AT LEAST 2029
    THEN `the sum` `the threshold of the year before` `updated by the rate of rise from` `the average wage on 1 January of the year before` `to` `the average wage as updated on 1 January of the year` `, reading a fall as` r
    ELSE `section 334(a)(2) updates the threshold by the average wage only from 1 January 2029`

@ref National Insurance Law s 334(a)(2) (source line 3607); the switch above
GIVEN `the year`                                       IS A NUMBER
      `the threshold of the year before`               IS A NUMBER
      `the average wage on 1 January of the year before` IS A NUMBER
      `the average wage as updated on 1 January of the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 334(a)(2) — the threshold on 1 January of` `the year` `from` `the threshold of the year before` `by the average wage from` `the average wage on 1 January of the year before` `to` `the average wage as updated on 1 January of the year` MEANS
    `s 334(a)(2) — the threshold on 1 January of` `the year` `from` `the threshold of the year before` `by the average wage from` `the average wage on 1 January of the year before` `to` `the average wage as updated on 1 January of the year`
        `, reading a fall as` `section 334(a) — the reading this row takes where the index or the average wage falls`

-- The threshold for a contribution month, by year. 2026 is the figure the National Insurance
-- Institute publishes (nii-il04-published-figures.l4). For 2027 and 2028 the index-updated figure
-- was not published when this row was made (2026-10-06), and from 2029 the wage-updated figure
-- depends on average wages not yet known: a caller who has the figure uses the s 337 rules that
-- take the threshold as an argument (nii-s337-rates.l4). Before 2026, the vintage refusal.
@ref National Insurance Law s 334(a), "מדרגת גבייה מופחתת" (source lines 3605-3607)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the reduced collection threshold for 2027 or 2028 had not been published when this encoding was made` MEANS
    REFUSE "the reduced collection threshold for 2027 or 2028 had not been published when this encoding was made"

@ref National Insurance Law s 334(a)(2) (source line 3607)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the reduced collection threshold from 2029 depends on average wages not known when this encoding was made` MEANS
    REFUSE "the reduced collection threshold from 2029 depends on average wages not known when this encoding was made"

@ref National Insurance Law s 334(a), "מדרגת גבייה מופחתת" (source lines 3605-3607); National Insurance Institute rates pages, fetched 2026-10-06
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 334(a) — the reduced collection threshold for a month in` `the year` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the year` AT LEAST 2029 THEN `the reduced collection threshold from 2029 depends on average wages not known when this encoding was made`
           IF `the year` AT LEAST 2027 THEN `the reduced collection threshold for 2027 or 2028 had not been published when this encoding was made`
           IF `the year` EQUALS   2026 THEN `the reduced collection threshold for 2026, as published by the National Insurance Institute`
           OTHERWISE                        `section 334(a) as it stood before 1 January 2026 is not in the deposited text`

§§ `334(b) — a person whose wage is fixed by a Law or a Knesset resolution`

-- src:3608 | (ב) לענין פרק זה רואים כעובד גם את מי ששכרו נקבע בחוק או בהחלטת הכנסת או על פיה, ואת החייב בתשלום השכר רואים כמעבידו.
-- "For this Chapter, a person whose wage is fixed in a Law or in a resolution of the Knesset or
-- under it is ALSO regarded as an employee, and the person liable to pay the wage as his employer."
-- So, for Chapter 15, "employee" is the s 1 definition OR this limb. Who pays the wage is a fact;
-- this row does not need a rule for it, and records it in a comment only.
@ref National Insurance Law s 334(b) (source line 3608), with s 1 "עובד" (source line 204)
GIVEN p IS A `A person who works`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 334(b) — the person is an employee for Chapter 15` p MEANS
        `s 1 — the person is an employee` p
    OR  p's `wage fixed in a Law or in or under a resolution of the Knesset`
